167-## 8. Planning Discipline
--
203-- goal-monitoring status memo when long-running analysis progress, solved signals, or stagnation triggers must remain explicit
204-- recovery / escalation checkpoint memo when blocked comparison state or fallback selection becomes the real control surface
205-- exploration frontier / hypothesis memo
206:- evidence target / retrieval-mode memo when route quality depends on grounded acquisition strategy
207-- source consultation ledger when the recommendation depends on which source groups were actually consulted or how public/private evidence was blended
208-- packet compliance report when the main design question is whether a control surface is missing rather than which option is best
209-- release evidence bundle memo when a recommendation must be attached to an actual promotion or hold decision
--
224-- do not let packet richness substitute for sharper comparison
225-- if a resource memo is used for concurrency-heavy options, preserve `parallelism cap`, `join cost`, or `saturation risk` explicitly rather than collapsing them into a generic cost note
226-- if the comparison is release-sensitive, preserve enough replay or evidence-bundle state that another reviewer can reproduce why the recommendation holds
227:- if route quality is the live concern, keep clarification-vs-exploration and fallback efficiency reviewable rather than burying them inside recommendation prose
