360-Keep one fallback path and one escalation trigger visible when uncertainty still matters.
361-If a benchmark-grade route claim lacks the required packet floor, downgrade the recommendation before route-quality language becomes stronger than the evidence.
362-Keep `scenario_id`, `run_id`, `cohort_id`, `trace_id`, and `artifact_version` stable when route-quality verdicts are compared across runs or cohorts.
363:When route quality is claimed as benchmarked, distinguish route review prose from a linked `Route-switch benchmark verdict`.
364-Keep `route-switch failure`, `late clarification`, and `failed fallback timing` independently diagnosable when the route itself is under review.
365-When route artifacts are joined, check precedence, compatibility, freshness, and completeness first; preserve upstream source IDs and `artifact_version` in the surviving verdict.
